{number: 40}
{title: Glory to His Name}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Down at the cross where my Savior died,
Down where for cleansing from [Eb7] sin I cried,
[Ab] There to my heart was the [Db] blood applied;
[Ab] Glory to [Eb7] His [Ab] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Glory to His name, [Db] glory to His [Ab] name;
There to my heart was the [Db] blood applied;
[Ab] Glory to [Eb7] His [Ab] name!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] I am so wondrously saved from sin,
Jesus so sweetly a-[Eb7] bides within,
[Ab] There at the cross where He [Db] took me in;
[Ab] Glory to [Eb7] His [Ab] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [Ab] precious fountain that saves from sin,
I am so glad I have [Eb7] entered in;
[Ab] There Jesus saves me and [Db] keeps me clean;
[Ab] Glory to [Eb7] His [Ab] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Ab] Come to this fountain so rich and sweet;
Cast your poor soul at the [Eb7] Savior’s feet;
[Ab] Plunge in today and be [Db] made complete;
[Ab] Glory to [Eb7] His [Ab] name!
{end_of_verse}
